Z||000000||MinnGreenGT||11-12-2001||01:47 PM||||I just posted this in the mall, but it might attract a little more attention here:<P>I'm a moron I guess. I ordered a set of 512MB PC133 SDRAM for my Apple G4/450 dual processor system.  Everything read correctly on the form when I ordered, but I hadn't researched Apple yet.  Afer attempting to install them in 3 Apple systems (unsuccessfully) I found that the new Mac firmware has a lockout for "out-of-spec" memory.  If the memory is not Apple Approved, it won't run in the system at all (doesn't get recognized).  The memory was successfully tested in another friends PC system- and they ran fine (but he was already maxed out on RAM).<P>Short end to long story. I'd rather not pay the 15% restocking fee through the place I ordered it... I paid $44.45 each for them (so I'd get $37.78 back - less my shipping cost).  I'd like to sell them for $40 ea- shipping included.<P>They are "brand-name" and come with a lifetime warranty (I'll include my original invoice too).  I'd suggest being sure that they work with your system before buying them ('cause I'm not interested in taking a return myself   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">).<P>------------------<BR>               <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif">  ||||reg||4
Z||000001||Loki||11-12-2001||02:33 PM||||AKK!! Thats expensice for memory   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Picked up 512 the other day for $22  Heh  But then agian had to take it back cause this GateWay MB doesnt recognize anything over 256 Ah well<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/fieroloki/lokisig1%20copy.jpg">  <BR>"All Fieros broke right now" :(||||reg||1
